{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1198922-thought-on-silver-fang-houses-and-the-litany","id":1198922,"title":"Thought on Silver Fang Houses and the Litany","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-23T18:32:25-07:00","id":1198922,"title":"Thought on Silver Fang Houses and the Litany","content":"I have, off and on over the years, wondered why the Silver Fangs have Houses - aside from the genre convention that they're nobles and therefor must have houses to jockey against each other - and one thing I keep coming back to again and again is that perhaps they originated based on differing ideas over which part of the Litany might have been considered more or most important to the House founder and, therefore, continues to play a big part of the House's overall identity, customs and renown recognition. <br /> <br /> In some cases, this is fairly easy to find a connection. House Wyrmfoe, for example, would be &quot;Combat the Wyrm wherever it Dwells and wherever it Breeds&quot; and House Unbreakable Hearth, given their name, might be &quot;Take No Action that Causes a Caern to be Violated&quot;. An argument might be made for House Wiseheart being &quot;Respect the Territory of Another&quot; given that they have always seemed to have a soft footprint in the Middle East and have managed to, if not co-exist then at least not antagonize the local Mokole, Bubasti and others. <br /> <br /> However, beyond that, I always have trouble figuring out possible connections. I've considered that the lost Roman House Conquering Claw might have been &quot;Submission to Those of Higher Station&quot; or &quot;First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station&quot;, and that Blood Red Crest might involve one or both of the other Station ones (respect those of lower/submit to those higher) as some sort of tie in to the Hindu caste system. I've also considered the possibility of Gleaming Eye, with their weird &quot;inquisition of the Wyrm tainted&quot; fixation, being focused on &quot;Do Not Suffer Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness&quot;. I've just never been able to really nail them down, especially with most of the others. Winter Snow might qualify for &quot;The Leader May Not Be Challenged in Wartime&quot; or &quot;Submission to those of Higher Station&quot;. The Ice Pack might, conceivably have taken &quot;Ye Shall Not Eat the Flesh of Humans&quot; to mean they should avoid humans and stay mostly Lupus. <br /> <br /> Anyway, it's just an idea I've been mulling over for some time, and thought some people here might be able to offer suggestions, opinions or other perspectives on the matter. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T18:45:49-07:00","id":1198927,"title":"","content":"I don't think they're ideological, just lineage based like real life royal houses perhaps with some kind of sacral kingship claiming support of a patron spirit to legitimize their house. Although I admit that some of the metaplot implies otherwise as I don't how Arkady Iceclaw would have legitimacy to seize the leadership of House Wyrmfoe. But I just identify that with bad writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T19:33:14-07:00","id":1198937,"title":"","content":"Yeah. The Silver Crown novel does have more than a few plot holes in it. (If it'd been up to me, Albrecht would've come back as the prodigal son to take control of the House<sup>1</sup>, but without the Silver Crown, leaving that for a Silver Fang - or even Shadow Lord or Child of Gaia - PC to find and then have Albrecht swear allegiance to said PC.) <br /> <br /> Anyway, most of the reason I keep coming back to this over the years is a desire to flesh the Houses out a little and give them a bit more character and depth. Part of it likely came from the tribe specific oaths/laws from Forsaken, which I thought was kind of cool. That and that it just seemed to fit so well with two or three of the Houses that my obsessive-compulsive personality won't let the fact that I can't fit the others into it so easily stop bugging me. <br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup><sub>Likely part of this consisting of an arranged marriage to the daughter/sister/niece of the leader of House Unbreakable Hearth as a means of getting their support. Just because that's how dynastic politics roll. </sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}